WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.335
Global navigation satellite systems, often shortened to G N S S, provide position, navigation, and timing services.

00:00:08.335 --> 00:00:11.264
GPS is one such system.

00:00:11.264 --> 00:00:20.049
Drones, vehicles, maps, communications, financial systems, power infrastructure, and many other technologies depend on satellite-derived position or time.

00:00:20.049 --> 00:00:26.582
Jamming is radio-frequency interference that degrades or blocks reception of weak satellite-navigation signals.

00:00:26.582 --> 00:00:34.467
It may cause lost lock, poor accuracy, warnings, or failure of features that depend on position.

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:40.098
Interference can be intentional, accidental, local, or caused by equipment faults.

00:00:40.098 --> 00:00:47.983
Spoofing is deceptive signal manipulation intended to make a receiver calculate an incorrect position or time.

00:00:47.983 --> 00:00:55.417
A receiver may continue reporting a confident-looking solution even though that solution disagrees with reality.

00:00:55.417 --> 00:00:59.697
These definitions describe effects, not a field diagnosis.

00:00:59.697 --> 00:01:10.285
Poor sky view, reflected signals, urban canyons, antenna problems, receiver faults, compass interference, software issues, or stale maps can create similar symptoms.

00:01:10.285 --> 00:01:14.565
One unusual reading does not prove an attack.

00:01:14.565 --> 00:01:20.647
For drone operators, the immediate question is not who caused the anomaly.

00:01:20.647 --> 00:01:28.982
It is whether navigation, automation, logs, and situational awareness remain trustworthy enough for safe flight and recovery.

00:01:28.982 --> 00:01:31.911
This course is defensive only.

00:01:31.911 --> 00:01:35.740
Never transmit interference or deceptive navigation signals.

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:47.680
The goal is to understand dependencies, recognize suspicious behavior, reduce reliance on uncertain automation, protect people and property, preserve evidence, and report through appropriate channels.
